# System Migrations

Spec: Migration
Purpose:
  Track migrations between architecture versions, decision versions,
  and skill versions. Each migration has a state, steps, and rollback
  strategy.

Owns: timeline/migrations.sdd

Migration Record:
  @migration.M-20
  from: repository-based payment
  to: domain service + event boundary
  steps:
    1. introduce interface
    2. migrate service
    3. migrate tests
    4. remove legacy
  rollback:
    revert to M-19 state

Migration States:
  PLANNED       — defined but not started
  IN_PROGRESS   — actively being worked
  PARTIAL       — some components migrated, system in mixed state
  COMPLETED     — fully migrated
  FAILED        — migration failed, rolled back
  ROLLED_BACK   — reverted to previous state

Partial Migration:
  Real projects rarely migrate everything at once.
  System records partial state:

  Payment:     100%
  Refund:      100%
  Settlement:  40%
  Architecture: MIGRATION_PARTIAL

  AI encounters this state and knows the system is not yet fully
  on the new architecture.

Why Legacy Exists:
  Legacy code paths carry historical decisions.
  AI must consult decision history before refactoring:

  legacy/payment.go
  → looks up → DEC-32
  → reason: provider did not support idempotency in 2025
  → AI understands: this code exists for a reason

Historical Decision Protection:
  Old decisions are preserved in historical context:

  DEC-32
  status: deprecated (in current context)
  but VALID_AT: 2025-06-10 (in historical context)

  AI must distinguish current truth from historical truth.

Compatibility:
  New skills may not work on older projects.

  @skill.architecture-v5
  requires:
    architecture >= 5

  Project at architecture=4 cannot use this skill.

Compatibility Matrix:
  | Component      | v1 | v2 | v3 |
  | -------------- | -: | -: | -: |
  | Skill A        |  ✅ |  ✅ |  ❌ |
  | Skill B        |  ✅ |  ✅ |  ✅ |
  | Architecture X |  ❌ |  ✅ |  ✅ |

  Compiler uses this matrix for skill selection.

Evolution Graph:
  Versions form an evolution graph, not always linear:

  Linear:
    v1 → v2 → v3 → v4

  Branch/merged:
        v2
       /  \
    v3a  v3b
       \  /
        v4

  Forked knowledge:
    @skill.api-design (global)
    @skill.api-design/payment (project A fork)
    @skill.api-design/internal (project B fork)
    relationship: FORKED_FROM

  Upstream/Downstream inheritance:
    GLOBAL SKILL → ORG SKILL → PROJECT SKILL → MODULE SKILL
    Project-local overrides allowed within project scope.

Inheritance Chain:
  @skill.api → @skill.rest-api → @skill.payment-api → @skill.refund-api

  Each layer adds rules; AI reads only delta rules at each layer.

  This aligns with token-efficient architecture: context is
  composed from versioned, scoped references rather than full copies.

State: +
